# Cline Rules — SalonBalance (Laravel 13, PHP 8.3)

## RULE 0 — TASK ORCHESTRATION (Always Default)

For any task touching more than 3 files, ALWAYS break into subtasks using new_task.

### Standard SalonBalance Subtask Split
When adding a new feature (e.g. Appointments, Invoices, Products):

```
new_task: "Create [Model] model with fillable, casts, relationships — read existing models first"
new_task: "Create migration for [table] — check database/migrations/ first for duplicates"
new_task: "Create [Model]Service with create/update/delete — read CustomerService for pattern"
new_task: "Create Store[Model]Request and Update[Model]Request in app/Http/Requests/[Model]/"
new_task: "Create [Model]Controller (thin, delegates to service) — read CustomersController for pattern"
new_task: "Create [Model]Resource — read CustomerResource for pattern"
new_task: "Add routes to routes/web.php — read existing routes first"
new_task: "Write Pest feature tests in tests/Feature/[Model]/ — cover store, update, delete, validation"
```

### Rules for Each Subtask
- Read only the files needed for that subtask (1-4 files max)
- Use write_to_file for all files under 300 lines
- Complete the file fully before finishing — no partial implementations
- Do NOT run migrations, npm install, or composer install unless explicitly instructed
- Do NOT modify files outside the subtask scope

---

## CRITICAL: File Existence — Check Before Creating

**Before creating ANY file**, verify it does not already exist using the filesystem tools.
If the file exists: READ it, understand it, then EDIT it — never overwrite or recreate it.

Files that commonly already exist in this project:
- `app/Models/Customer.php` ✅ exists
- `app/Models/Treatment.php` ✅ exists
- `app/Models/User.php` ✅ exists
- `app/Http/Controllers/CustomersController.php` ✅ exists
- `app/Http/Controllers/TreatmentsController.php` ✅ exists
- `app/Http/Resources/CustomerResource.php` ✅ exists
- `app/Providers/AppServiceProvider.php` ✅ exists
- `routes/web.php` ✅ exists
- `routes/console.php` ✅ exists

---

## FORBIDDEN Commands — Never Run These

```
laravel new          # NEVER — project already exists
php artisan make:*   # NEVER without checking target file does not exist first
composer create-project  # NEVER
npm create           # NEVER
```

Before running `php artisan make:migration`, check `database/migrations/` for existing migrations on the same table. If a migration already handles that table, **edit the existing migration** (if not yet run) or **create a new additive migration** (e.g. `add_email_to_customers_table`).

---

## Project Structure — Always Follow This Layout

```
app/
├── Actions/          # Single-purpose action classes (e.g. CreateCustomerAction)
├── Data/             # DTOs — typed data transfer objects
├── Enums/            # PHP 8.1+ backed enums
├── Http/
│   ├── Controllers/  # Thin controllers — delegate to Actions/Services
│   ├── Requests/     # Form Requests for ALL validation — never validate in controllers
│   └── Resources/    # API Resources for ALL responses — never return raw models
├── Models/           # Eloquent models
├── Policies/         # Authorization policies — one per model
├── Providers/        # Service providers
└── Services/         # Business logic and orchestration
database/
├── factories/        # Model factories
├── migrations/       # One migration per schema change
└── seeders/          # Database seeders
routes/
├── web.php           # Web routes
└── api.php           # API routes (create if needed)
tests/
├── Feature/          # Pest feature tests
└── Unit/             # Pest unit tests
```

---

## Controllers — Enterprise Rules

**Controllers must be thin.** No business logic inside controllers.

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Http\Controllers;

use App\Http\Requests\Customer\StoreCustomerRequest;
use App\Http\Requests\Customer\UpdateCustomerRequest;
use App\Http\Resources\CustomerResource;
use App\Models\Customer;
use App\Services\CustomerService;
use Illuminate\Http\RedirectResponse;
use Illuminate\Http\Resources\Json\AnonymousResourceCollection;
use Illuminate\View\View;

class CustomersController extends Controller
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly CustomerService $customerService,
    ) {}

    public function index(): View|AnonymousResourceCollection
    {
        $customers = Customer::query()->with('treatments')->paginate(25);

        return view('customers.index', compact('customers'));
    }

    public function store(StoreCustomerRequest $request): RedirectResponse
    {
        $this->customerService->create($request->validated());

        return redirect()->route('customers.index')->with('success', 'Customer created.');
    }
}
```

Rules:
- Always use **model binding**: `Customer $customer` not `string $id`
- Always use **Form Request** classes for validation — never `$request->validate()` directly in controller
- Always declare **return types**
- Always use `declare(strict_types=1)` at the top of every file
- Inject services via constructor with `private readonly`
- Use `compact()` or named array keys for view data

---

## Models — Enterprise Rules

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Models;

use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Factories\HasFactory;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Relations\HasMany;

class Customer extends Model
{
    use HasFactory;

    protected $fillable = [
        'name',
        'telephone_number',
        'street_address',
    ];

    protected function casts(): array
    {
        return [
            'created_at' => 'datetime',
            'updated_at' => 'datetime',
        ];
    }

    public function treatments(): HasMany
    {
        return $this->hasMany(Treatment::class);
    }
}
```

Rules:
- Always use `HasFactory` trait
- Always type-hint relationship return types (`HasMany`, `BelongsTo`, `BelongsToMany`, etc.)
- Use `casts()` method (not `$casts` property) for PHP 8+ compatibility
- Never use `::all()` — use `::query()->...` with pagination
- Use Eloquent scopes for reusable query logic
- Use `$fillable` (not `$guarded = []`)

---

## Form Requests — Required for All Validation

Never put `$request->validate()` in a controller. Always create a Form Request.

```
app/Http/Requests/Customer/StoreCustomerRequest.php
app/Http/Requests/Customer/UpdateCustomerRequest.php
app/Http/Requests/Treatment/StoreTreatmentRequest.php
```

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Http\Requests\Customer;

use Illuminate\Foundation\Http\FormRequest;

class StoreCustomerRequest extends FormRequest
{
    public function authorize(): bool
    {
        return true;
    }

    public function rules(): array
    {
        return [
            'name'             => ['required', 'string', 'max:255'],
            'telephone_number' => ['required', 'string', 'max:50'],
            'street_address'   => ['required', 'string', 'max:255'],
        ];
    }
}
```

---

## Services — Business Logic Layer

Business logic belongs in `app/Services/`, never in controllers or models.

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Services;

use App\Models\Customer;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\DB;

class CustomerService
{
    public function create(array $validated): Customer
    {
        return DB::transaction(static function () use ($validated): Customer {
            return Customer::create($validated);
        });
    }

    public function update(Customer $customer, array $validated): Customer
    {
        $customer->update($validated);

        return $customer->fresh();
    }

    public function delete(Customer $customer): void
    {
        $customer->delete();
    }
}
```

---

## API Resources — Required for All API Responses

Never return a raw Model or Collection from an API route. Always use a Resource.

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Http\Resources;

use Illuminate\Http\Request;
use Illuminate\Http\Resources\Json\JsonResource;

class CustomerResource extends JsonResource
{
    public function toArray(Request $request): array
    {
        return [
            'id'               => $this->id,
            'name'             => $this->name,
            'telephone_number' => $this->telephone_number,
            'street_address'   => $this->street_address,
            'treatments'       => TreatmentResource::collection($this->whenLoaded('treatments')),
            'created_at'       => $this->created_at->toISOString(),
        ];
    }
}
```

---

## Migrations — Strict Rules

Before creating a migration:
1. List all files in `database/migrations/`
2. Check if any migration already creates or modifies the target table
3. If a `create_X_table` migration exists: do NOT create another — edit it if not yet run, or write an additive `add_column_to_X_table` migration

Migration naming:
- Create: `create_customers_table`
- Add column: `add_email_to_customers_table`
- Rename: `rename_phone_to_telephone_in_customers_table`
- Drop: `drop_legacy_orders_table`

Never create duplicate `create_X_table` migrations. The database has these tables already:
- `users`, `cache`, `jobs` (default Laravel)
- `customers`
- `treatments`

---

## PHP 8.3 Standards — Always Apply

```php
declare(strict_types=1);          // top of every file
```

Use:
- **Typed properties**: `public string $name;`
- **Return types**: always declared, use `void`, `never`, `mixed` where appropriate  
- **Named arguments**: `Customer::create(name: $name)` for clarity
- **Enums** for fixed sets of values (e.g. status fields): `app/Enums/`
- **Readonly properties**: `public readonly string $name`
- **Match expressions** over switch statements
- **Nullsafe operator**: `$user?->profile?->avatar`
- **First-class callable syntax**: `array_map($this->transform(...), $items)`

Never use:
- `array` type hints without generics in PHPDoc
- Inline `if/else` for complex logic — extract to methods
- Magic numbers — use named constants or enums
- `var_dump`, `dd`, `die` in committed code

---

## Testing — Pest (Required)

Every new feature or bug fix must have a Pest test.

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

use App\Models\Customer;

it('creates a customer with valid data', function (): void {
    $response = $this->post(route('customers.store'), [
        'name'             => 'Jane Doe',
        'telephone_number' => '0612345678',
        'street_address'   => 'Main Street 1',
    ]);

    $response->assertRedirect(route('customers.index'));
    $this->assertDatabaseHas('customers', ['name' => 'Jane Doe']);
});

it('fails validation when name is missing', function (): void {
    $this->post(route('customers.store'), [])
        ->assertSessionHasErrors(['name']);
});
```

Test file location:
- Feature tests: `tests/Feature/`
- Unit tests: `tests/Unit/`
- Organized by domain: `tests/Feature/Customers/`, `tests/Feature/Treatments/`

Run tests with: `php artisan test` or `./vendor/bin/pest`

---

## Blade Templates — Conventions

- Store in `resources/views/` organized by domain: `customers/`, `treatments/`
- Use Tailwind CSS v4 (already installed via `@tailwindcss/vite`)
- Use Blade components for reusable UI: `resources/views/components/`
- Never put PHP business logic in Blade — only display logic
- Always escape output: `{{ $var }}` not `{!! $var !!}` unless explicitly safe HTML

---

## Error Handling

- Use Laravel's exception handler — never `try/catch` for control flow
- For expected failures, use `abort(404)` or `throw new ModelNotFoundException()`
- Log unexpected errors: `Log::error('message', ['context' => $data])`
- Return consistent error responses from API endpoints using `response()->json(['message' => '...'], 422)`

---

## Security Rules

- Never commit secrets — all credentials in `.env` only
- Never expose internal IDs in URLs if sensitivity requires it — use UUIDs
- Always authorize actions via Policies: `$this->authorize('update', $customer)`
- Validate ALL user input via Form Requests
- Use `$fillable` on every model — never `$guarded = []`
- Rate limit sensitive routes

---

## What This Project Is

**SalonBalance** — A salon management application.

Existing domain:
- `Customer` — has name, telephone_number, street_address
- `Treatment` — belongs to Customer, has name, price, version

Stack:
- Laravel 13 / PHP 8.3
- MySQL (`SalonBalance` database)
- Tailwind CSS v4
- Vite 8
- Pest 4 for testing
- `laravel/pail` for log tailing
